  "findings": [
    "Pelagus does not use BIP47 notification transactions; it announces channels with notify() on a Quai-ledger mailbox contract and receivers read getNotifications(receiverCode).",
    "The Rust SDK discovered the Pelagus sender code from the mailbox with a typed contract call, validated it, registered the channel and found both outputs (10 Qi and 5 Qi) at the first two receive indexes with default gap-50 scanning.",
    "A quai_call with the contract's own address as from was rejected with -32000; an account caller succeeds.",
    "Mailbox announcements are unauthenticated public data: anyone can notify any receiver, so codes must be validated and channel scanning bounded.",
    "A Pelagus-compatible notify from the Rust SDK mined at block 10098750 using 243807 gas (9.33 QUAI); the mailbox then listed our code for the Pelagus receiver.",
    "A 1 Qi return payment to the Pelagus channel was prepared and signed spending the 5 Qi output received from Pelagus with its BIP47 receive key (fee 40 Qits).",
    "The 1 Qi return mined at block 10098870; its output is indexed at the Pelagus channel send address and mined bytes matched custody."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Pelagus-side display of the returned 1 Qi is confirmed by the user, not by this harness.",
    "The sender code is inferred from the mailbox; the user did not separately confirm it."
  ],
